{"Backup code comparisons remove dashes but do not trim whitespace or normalize case, so valid codes can be rejected when users enter uppercase A-F or paste with surrounding spaces/newlines": 0.9464035630226135, "JSON.parse() is called on decrypted backupCodes in disable-2FA endpoint and credentials authorize flow without error handling, which can throw and fail the request with a 500 instead of a controlled auth error if data is malformed/corrupted": 0.9757081866264343, "After 2FA is successfully enabled server-side, onEnable() callback is only called when user clicks explicit Close button on backup codes step - dismissing dialog via ESC, X button, or backdrop click bypasses onEnable() leaving UI showing 2FA as disabled while it is actually enabled on server": 0.9841917753219604, "Blob URL created for backup code download via URL.createObjectURL is never revoked when modal is closed via cancel or close buttons, causing a memory leak each time the modal is opened and closed": 0.7790316939353943, "Setup.ts API endpoint returns backup codes in plaintext in response body before user has confirmed 2FA setup by entering a valid TOTP code, creating unnecessary exposure window where codes are transmitted before 2FA is actually enabled": 0.7875933647155762}